1
00:00:01,759 --> 00:00:06,158
Chapter 33. The specs cinder.

2
00:00:06,159 --> 00:00:10,399
Concerning the officers of the whalecraft, this seems as good a place

3
00:00:10,400 --> 00:00:15,918
as any to set down a little domestic peculiarity on shipboard, arising from

4
00:00:15,919 --> 00:00:21,199
the existence of the harpooner class of officers, a class unknown, of course, in

5
00:00:21,200 --> 00:00:23,999
any other marine than the whale fleet.

6
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:29,118
The large importance attached to the harpooner's vocation is evinced by the

7
00:00:29,119 --> 00:00:34,877
fact that originally in the old Dutch fishery two centuries or more ago, the

8
00:00:34,878 --> 00:00:39,199
command of a whale ship was not wholly lodged in the person now called the

9
00:00:39,200 --> 00:00:45,039
captain, but was divided between him and an officer called the specsinder.

10
00:00:45,040 --> 00:00:47,999
Literally, this word means fat cutter.

11
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:53,118
Usage, however, in time made it equivalent to chief harpooner. In those

12
00:00:53,119 --> 00:00:57,438
days, the captain's authority was restricted to the navigation and general

13
00:00:57,439 --> 00:01:02,158
management of the vessel, while over the whale hunting department and all its

14
00:01:02,159 --> 00:01:07,999
concerns, the specs cinder or chief harpooner reigns supreme. In the British

15
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:13,598
Greenland fishery, under the corrupted title of specioner, this old Dutch

16
00:01:13,599 --> 00:01:19,039
official is still retained, but his former dignity is sadly abridged. At

17
00:01:19,040 --> 00:01:23,438
present he ranks simply as senior harpooner and as such is but one of the

18
00:01:23,439 --> 00:01:27,039
captain's more inferior sub altern.

19
00:01:27,040 --> 00:01:32,239
Nevertheless, as upon good conduct of the harpooners the success of a whailing

20
00:01:32,240 --> 00:01:37,758
voyage largely depends, and since in the American fishery he is not only an

21
00:01:37,759 --> 00:01:42,399
important officer in the boat, but under certain circumstances, night watches on

22
00:01:42,400 --> 00:01:47,359
a whailing ground, the command of the ship's deck is also his. Therefore, the

23
00:01:47,360 --> 00:01:52,079
grand political maxim of the sea demands that he should nominally live apart from

24
00:01:52,080 --> 00:01:56,636
the men before the mast and be in some way distinguished as their professional

25
00:01:56,637 --> 00:02:03,519
superior, though always by them familiarly regarded as their social equal.

26
00:02:03,520 --> 00:02:09,039
Now, the grand distinction drawn between officer and man at sea is this. The

27
00:02:09,040 --> 00:02:11,839
first lives aft, the last forward.

28
00:02:11,840 --> 00:02:15,999
Hence, in whale ships and merchantmen alike, the mates have their quarters

29
00:02:16,000 --> 00:02:21,359
with the captain, and so too in most of the American whalers, the harpooners are

30
00:02:21,360 --> 00:02:23,839
lodged in the afterpart of the ship.

31
00:02:23,840 --> 00:02:28,079
That is to say, they take their meals in the captain's cabin and sleep in a place

32
00:02:28,080 --> 00:02:31,199
indirectly communicating with it.

33
00:02:31,200 --> 00:02:35,438
Though the long period of a southern whailing voyage, by far the longest of

34
00:02:35,439 --> 00:02:41,199
all voyages now or ever made by man, the peculiar perils of it, and the community

35
00:02:41,200 --> 00:02:45,839
of interest prevailing among a company, all of whom, high or low, depend for

36
00:02:45,840 --> 00:02:50,717
their profits, not upon fixed wages, but upon their common luck, together with

37
00:02:50,718 --> 00:02:55,839
their common vigilance, intrepidity, and hard work. Though all these things do in

38
00:02:55,840 --> 00:03:00,079
some cases tend to be get a less rigorous discipline than in merchant men

39
00:03:00,080 --> 00:03:05,438
generally. Yet never mind how much like an old Mesopotamian family these

40
00:03:05,439 --> 00:03:10,956
whalemen may in some primitive instances live together. For all that the

41
00:03:10,957 --> 00:03:15,758
punctilious externals at least of the quarter deck are seldom materially

42
00:03:15,759 --> 00:03:19,118
relaxed and in no instance done away.

43
00:03:19,119 --> 00:03:23,679
Indeed, many are the Nantucket ships in which you will see the skipper parading

44
00:03:23,680 --> 00:03:29,839
his quarter deck with an elated grandeur not surpassed in any military navy. Nay,

45
00:03:29,840 --> 00:03:35,118
extorting almost as much outward homage as if he wore the imperial purple, not

46
00:03:35,119 --> 00:03:38,318
the shabiest of pilot cloth.

47
00:03:38,319 --> 00:03:42,717
And though of all men the moody captain of the Peekquad was the least given to

48
00:03:42,718 --> 00:03:47,758
that sort of shallowest assumption, and though the only homage he ever exacted

49
00:03:47,759 --> 00:03:53,359
was implicit instantaneous obedience, though he required no man to remove the

50
00:03:53,360 --> 00:03:57,359
shoes from his feet stepping upon the quarter deck, and though there were

51
00:03:57,360 --> 00:04:01,598
times when, owing to peculiar circumstances connected with events

52
00:04:01,599 --> 00:04:06,557
hereafter to be detailed, he addressed them in unusual terms, whether of

53
00:04:06,558 --> 00:04:11,918
condescension or in terorum or otherwise. Yet even Captain Ahab was by

54
00:04:11,919 --> 00:04:18,478
no means unobservant of the paramount forms and usages of the sea. Nor perhaps

55
00:04:18,479 --> 00:04:23,679
will it fail to be eventually perceived that behind those forms and usages, as

56
00:04:23,680 --> 00:04:29,598
it were, he sometimes masked himself, incidentally making use of them for

57
00:04:29,599 --> 00:04:35,359
